{C_\tau D\log D} \frac{1}{\sqrt{\wtilde D-2}}
\end{align*}
Since From Theorem \ref{thm:Step1} we have that $\alpha \leq \sqrt{ 1/D}$, and thus 
$( 1 + \alpha)^{\wtilde D}$ is bounded for any $D$. Thus, we have that for $C_\tau$ large enough, 
\begin{align}
